WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.270
- Do people still freak out?

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:03.080
Like my thing, it's like
everybody comes come up

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:04.750
and yells, "Ah, Kelly Clarkson!"

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:07.568
Do people, and this is
your Hamilton, so it's like

00:00:07.568 --> 00:00:09.440
do people always come up to you

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.290
and are just like talking to
you non-stop about Hamilton?

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:12.570
Because it was such a movement.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:14.950
I feel like when I was a
kid, and Rent came out,

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.200
how popular that was and how it blew up,

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.740
that's what Hamilton
is for this generation.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.400
It's just like enormous.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.310
- It was that, and it, no,
it was weird, you know.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.660
Davide used to say this
thing, this, I love,

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.157
that Davide used to say,
right outside the stage door,

00:00:28.157 --> 00:00:30.582
"You were a beetle for a
block", you know what I mean?

00:00:30.582 --> 00:00:31.415
(laughing)

00:00:31.415 --> 00:00:33.540
Once you crossed 8th Avenue
it kind of died down,

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.940
but it took it took time to get used

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.160
to getting recognized at the
airport and stuff like that.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.908
I'd be looking behind me like,
"Who are they looking at?".

00:00:40.908 --> 00:00:44.550
But it was, you know, a huge phenomenon.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.353
It changed our lives,
you know what I mean?

00:00:46.353 --> 00:00:48.000
- [Kelly] Yeah the
trajectory of your, yeah.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.650
But it also gave just
really talented people

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.710
a chance and opportunity
to really showcase all

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:54.543
that you are capable of.

00:00:54.543 --> 00:00:55.700
Like how he wrote those songs.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.740
I mean, my husband is a full on cowboy,

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:01.090
like raises cattle, road
bulls, like that kind of guy.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.200
Tears.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.740
We went to New York and he was like,

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:05.829
he was looking around going (mumbles)

00:01:05.829 --> 00:01:06.662
(laughing)

00:01:06.662 --> 00:01:10.050
He was like crying, like it was so good,

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:12.810
just such a great moment
in time, but I'm so glad

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:15.730
that you have the music
now that you're doing now.

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:18.263
I love that you're transitioning.

